Q: Issue to scroll tbody on IE 9 (tbody&#39;s height = height-line) A: <p>Here is a shorter answer that allows you to scroll the table with a fixed header in ie9.</p>

<p>Add a conditional div around the table</p>

<pre><code>&lt;!--[if lte IE 9]&gt;
&lt;div class="old_ie_wrapper"&gt;
&lt;!--&lt;![endif]--&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
...
&lt;!--[if lte IE 9]&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;!--&lt;![endif]--&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Add the following styles for ie9</p>

<pre><code>    .old_ie_wrapper {
        height: 500px;
        overflow: auto;
    }

        .old_ie_wrapper tbody {
            height: auto;
        }

        .old_ie_wrapper thead tr {
            position: absolute;
        }

        .old_ie_wrapper tbody tr:first-child {
            height: 67px;
            vertical-align: bottom;
        }
</code></pre>

<p>You will have to adjust the heights and probably other properties based on your table.</p>

